-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/8 (19.5.2024), ניכוי המקדמה מכוח ההסכם הקיבוצי מיום
-- 12.09.2023 לעובדי הוראה בחטיבות העליונות
-- How the owners of upper-secondary schools deduct the advance paid under
-- the collective agreement of 12.9.2023: six equal parts in six consecutive
-- monthly salaries from May 2024's, and the balance in the final settlement
-- of an employee who leaves first.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time is counted in SALARY MONTHS from April 2024's (0): May 2024's salary,
-- paid on 1.6.2024, is 1, and the sixth consecutive salary, October 2024's, is 6.
`May 2024's salary` MEANS 1

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/8 — ניכוי המקדמה מכוח ההסכם הקיבוצי מיום 12.09.2023`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13 The letterhead, date, reference number, addressees (the owners of upper-secondary schools), greeting, subject line and the earlier circular it follows (תשפ"ד/4); no rule.

-- The sources the owners act on: the collective agreement of 12.9.2023
-- (published in circular תשפ"ד/4) and the Treasury wage commissioner's
-- instructions of 17.3.2024 and 9.4.2024, linked from the last paragraph
-- (meyda.education.gov.il/files/Sherut/mikdama.pdf). They are not restated
-- here; where they set more than this circular says, they are an input.
@ref akn:preamble/p14 akn:art_4/p2
ASSUME `the wage commissioner's instructions of 17.3.2024 and 9.4.2024` IS A STRING
@desc The Treasury wage commissioner's instructions on deducting the advance, linked from the circular (mikdama.pdf); not restated in the circular.

@desc A teaching employee who was paid the advance, as far as this circular asks.
DECLARE `employee paid the advance` HAS
    `advance received`              IS A NUMBER  @desc the advance the employee was paid under the agreement of 12.9.2023
    `last salary month employed`    IS A NUMBER  @desc the last salary month (May 2024 = 1) in which the employee is employed by the employer; 99 if employment continues

@ref akn:art_2
`the number of equal payments` MEANS 6

@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_2
GIVEN e IS AN `employee paid the advance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `one monthly deduction` e IS
    e's `advance received` DIVIDED BY `the number of equal payments`

-- The salary months that carry a deduction: six consecutive from May 2024's.
@ref akn:art_2 akn:art_3
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a deduction falls in salary month` m IF
        m AT LEAST `May 2024's salary`
    AND m AT MOST `May 2024's salary` PLUS `the number of equal payments` MINUS 1

GIVEN e IS AN `employee paid the advance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leaves before the six months end` e IF
    e's `last salary month employed` LESS THAN `May 2024's salary` PLUS `the number of equal payments` MINUS 1

GIVEN e IS AN `employee paid the advance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deductions made while employed` e IS
    max 0 (min `the number of equal payments` (e's `last salary month employed` MINUS `May 2024's salary` PLUS 1))

-- Notwithstanding the above, an employee who leaves the employer before the
-- six months end has the balance deducted in the final settlement.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN e IS AN `employee paid the advance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the balance deducted in the final settlement` e IS
    IF `leaves before the six months end` e
    THEN e's `advance received`
         MINUS `one monthly deduction` e TIMES `deductions made while employed` e
    ELSE 0

DECLARE `deduction action` IS ONE OF
    `deduct a part of the advance` HAS `part deducted` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct the balance in the final settlement` HAS `balance deducted` IS A NUMBER

-- The six deductions as a chain of monthly duties: each one in its own
-- salary month, the first in May 2024's (paid 1.6.2024).
@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_2 akn:art_3
GIVEN `part` IS A NUMBER, `parts left` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `deduction action`
DECIDE `the six monthly deductions` `part` `parts left` IS
    IF `parts left` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `deduct a part of the advance` d PROVIDED d EQUALS `part`
         WITHIN 1
         HENCE `the six monthly deductions` `part` (`parts left` MINUS 1)
         LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "sections 2–3: the advance is deducted in six equal parts in six consecutive salaries from May 2024's"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN e IS AN `employee paid the advance`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `deduction action`
DECIDE `the balance on leaving` e IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `deduct the balance in the final settlement` b PROVIDED b EQUALS `the balance deducted in the final settlement` e
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 4: the balance of the advance is deducted in the final settlement"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: the signatures and the copies list; no rule.

-- Examples. The advances are those circular תשפ"ד/4 printed for a full position.
`a reform teacher who stays` MEANS
    `employee paid the advance` WITH
        `advance received`           IS 2400
        `last salary month employed` IS 99

`a non-reform teacher who leaves after July 2024` MEANS
    `employee paid the advance` WITH
        `advance received`           IS 1500
        `last salary month employed` IS 3

#ASSERT `one monthly deduction` `a reform teacher who stays` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `one monthly deduction` `a non-reform teacher who leaves after July 2024` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `a deduction falls in salary month` 1 AND `a deduction falls in salary month` 6
#ASSERT NOT `a deduction falls in salary month` 7
#ASSERT `the balance deducted in the final settlement` `a reform teacher who stays` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the balance deducted in the final settlement` `a non-reform teacher who leaves after July 2024` EQUALS 750

#TRACE `the six monthly deductions` 400 6 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct a part of the advance` 400 AT 1
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct a part of the advance` 400 AT 2
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct a part of the advance` 400 AT 3
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct a part of the advance` 400 AT 4
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct a part of the advance` 400 AT 5
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct a part of the advance` 400 AT 6
#TRACE `the balance on leaving` `a non-reform teacher who leaves after July 2024` AT 3 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct the balance in the final settlement` 750 AT 4
